    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup anchored by two high-ceiling plays: **Luis Robert Jr.** (76.18) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (75.09). **Luis Robert Jr.** is our premier start, benefiting from a massive +16% park factor boost and a favorable platoon advantage against Suarez, creating a profile that balances power with his critical elite speed potential. Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** remains an automatic start, capitalizing on a soft matchup against Lynch IV (4.16 xERA), where his consistency and favorable order placement in the three-hole provide a high floor for counting stats. While **Kyle Tucker** is batting lower than ideal at the eighth spot, his 70.68 score reflects an elite matchup against a weak starter in Kent, J, whose 5.48 xERA offers massive potential for multi-hit production and RBI opportunities, forcing him into the lineup despite the suboptimal order placement.\n\nThe most notable bench decision today was the exclusion of **Nasim Nunez** (42.64), who represents the highest-scoring player left on the pine. While **Nasim Nunez** provides high-leverage speed\u2014an asset we prioritize\u2014the optimizer ultimately faded him due to a poor lineup spot (hitting ninth) and a difficult matchup against Snell, whose 3.30 xERA limits the potential for sustained rallies. We are also monitoring the volatility surrounding **Gunnar Henderson** (61.25); while he benefits from the same park factors as **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Coby Mayo**, his score was hampered by a -15% drag from the platoon disadvantage against Suarez. However, his elite talent level keeps him firmly in the \"Strong\" start tier, as his ability to negate splits is superior to the marginal options currently benched.",
